# Vendored 9front arm64 C compiler `7c`
# (https://github.com/9front/9front @ 350266104f1fed81c78c3d05fa44f523bec0ae4d,
# branch "front", pinned 2026-10-31).
#
# 7c is Harvey's aarch64 compiler: the project's tree name for the
# architecture is `aarch64` (D-01: arm64 == aarch64, the same ISA);
# the tool letter stays 7. Imported as a temporary bridge on the way to
# the r9 kernel — see .planning/ROADMAP.md Phase 2.
#
# What was imported: sys/src/cmd/7c/ wholesale (including 7.out.h, the
# object-format header shared with 7a, 7l and libmach's 7obj.c).
#
# Local modifications vs upstream (D-13: drift is shimmed in vendored
# files only — Harvey's shared cc frontend is untouched):
#   * math.h — added; two-line unix-SDK shadow copied verbatim from
#     6c/math.h. Without it plan9port's u.h pulls the host SDK math.h,
#     whose round(double)/log2(double) collide with cc.h's
#     round(long,int)/log2(uvlong).
#   * gc.h — swcmp declaration changed to the const-qualified form
#     `int swcmp(const void*, const void*)`, matching Harvey's
#     cc/pswt.c definition (and 6c/gc.h).
#   * sgen.c / cgen.c / txt.c — 9front's rotate-fold optimization
#     excised (3 sites): the rolor(n) call in sgen.c, the `case OROL:`
#     label in cgen.c, and the OROL case block in txt.c. Harvey's shared
#     frontend has no OROL node producer, so the vendored consumers are
#     dead code; removing them keeps the shared frontend untouched.
#     Zero functional loss (no rotate fusion).
#   * txt.c — thestring set to the aarch64 arch name (donor value was
#     arm64). Harvey's host-built tools resolve includes as
#     /{thestring}/include (cc/lex.c), and Harvey's tree names the arch
#     dir aarch64.
#   * enam.c — generated from vendored 7.out.h by the donor mkenam ed
#     script and committed (6c precedent: no enam.c rule in the mkfile).
#     Regenerate only when 7.out.h's opcode enum changes.
#   * mkfile — rewritten in Harvey idiom (6c/mkfile model, minus div;
#     donor's used <../cc/mkfile.port which Harvey lacks).
#   * BUILD — new; host build via plan9port 9c/9l (6c/BUILD pattern,
#     no -static, no div.c).
#
